[17.643175, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[17.674789, "o", "S1  Leaked Bedrock API key (LLMjacking)\r\n    A long-term Bedrock API key leaked from a build log. From 14:05 someone outside the company uses it: recon, a logging check, a failed attempt to delete invocation logging, then 90 minutes of large Converse, ConverseStream and bedrock-mantle calls.\r\n\r\nS2  Jailbroken customer bot\r\n    A signed-in customer spends 12 minutes trying to jailbreak the support bot. The guardrail blocks six attempts; one gets through and the answer contains the system prompt's canary.\r\n\r\nS3  Hijacked agent\r\n    A rollback pipeline puts the agent gateway's policy engine back in LOG_ONLY. Eight minutes later a hidden instruction in ticket 5120 makes the agent email ticket data outside the company and reset the CEO's MFA. The policy engine said DENY both times.\r\n\r\nS4  Denial of wallet through the app\r\n    A scripted sign-up account sends 300 maximum-length chats in 50 minutes. Every call is made by the app's own role, so AWS sees one busy app, not one abusive user.\r\n\r\nS5  Poisoned knowledge base\r\n    At 03:10 a contractor upload role writes a fake 'VPN support update' into the knowledge base source bucket and starts an ingestion job itself. From 09:00 the support bot sends customers to an outside 'VPN support line'.\r\n\r\n"]
